# Does a tamed Spook caster still demoralize its own master?
#
# bd inc-9mhh. Spook is a mobile field centred on its caster, radius 3, that
# gives every creature inside it a -2 morale penalty to all rolls
# (lib/wspells.irh:967-976). It carries EF_CASTER_IMMUNE, so the caster is
# spared, and it does NOT carry EF_ALLIES_IMMUNE, so everyone on the caster's
# own side is not. A night hunter taken as a companion therefore stands beside
# its master and holds him at -2 for as long as it lives, and the penalty is
# permanent because the field is EF_PERSISTANT.
#
# THE ORACLE is the character sheet's Hit line, which prints the morale term.
# The run measures four states in order, and the first of them is the control:
#
#   1 no bat                       Hit 6
#   2 a HOSTILE night hunter       Hit 4    <- must stay 4 after any fix
#   3 the same bat, tamed, and the player walked out of its radius   Hit 6
#   4 walked back in, still tamed  Hit 4 before the fix, 6 after
#
# State 2 is what stops a "fix" that merely switches the spell off from
# passing. State 3 proves the walk really leaves the field, so state 4 is a
# fresh entry and not a stale stati nobody recomputed.
#
# Freeze Monsters is on so the bat neither attacks nor follows. It still
# raises its aura, because Monster::Initialize runs PreBuff when the creature
# is created, not on its turn.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Explore Mode -- yes
i       # Race:  [i] Orc
a       # Subrace: [a] Orc (Standard)
j       # Class: [j] Warrior -- a class with Ride and no spell menus
a       # Attributes: the first offered set
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
a       # Personality archetype
@until "Things in View" ESC

@dump:no-bat

w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
# The list draws no cursor a screen dump can see, so this counts rows:
# Freeze Monsters is the eleventh, and the cursor opens on the first.
DOWN*10
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "night hunter"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:hostile-bat

w
@choose "Make Player Master of Monster"
RIGHT ENTER

# Out of the radius, then back into it. Four squares is past a radius of 3.
LEFT LEFT LEFT LEFT LEFT
@dump:walked-away
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT
@dump:walked-back

@quit
